[Event "Queen's Gambit Declined - complete development · White"]
[Site "Chess for Anki"]
[Date "2026.11.16"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Learner"]
[Black "Saved line"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 { White places a pawn on d4, taking central space and opening the bishop's diagonal. } 1... d5 { Black occupies d5 and prevents White from taking the entire centre without a challenge. } 2. c4 { White attacks d5 with the c-pawn. The pawn exchange is a way to influence the centre. } 2... e6 { Black supports d5 with e6 instead of taking c4. This is the Queen's Gambit Declined. } 3. Nc3 { White develops the knight to c3 and adds pressure to d5. } 3... Nf6 { Black develops the knight to f6, supporting d5 and preparing to castle. } 4. Nf3 { White develops the other knight and protects the pawn on d4. } 4... Be7 { Black brings the bishop to e7 and clears the way for kingside castling. } 5. Bg5 { White develops the bishop actively to g5. The bishop on e7 means there is no direct pin of the knight to the queen here. } 5... O-O { Black castles kingside, placing the king behind its pawns. } 6. e3 { White supports d4 with e3 and opens the diagonal for the bishop on f1. } 6... h6 { Black asks the bishop on g5 to decide whether to retreat or exchange. } 7. Bh4 { White keeps the bishop with Bh4. The bishop remains aimed along the kingside diagonal. } 7... b6 { Black prepares to develop the bishop to b7, where it can influence the central diagonal. } 8. cxd5 { White exchanges the c-pawn for the pawn on d5, beginning to clarify the centre. } 8... Nxd5 { Black recaptures with the knight, putting a piece on the central square d5. } 9. Bxe7 { White exchanges the bishop for Black's bishop on e7. } 9... Qxe7 { Black recaptures with the queen and keeps the material balance. } 10. Nxd5 { White exchanges the knight on c3 for the knight on d5. } 10... exd5 { Black recaptures with the e-pawn. The pawn structure now gives both sides a new set of central plans. } 11. Bd3 { White develops the bishop to d3, aiming toward Black's kingside and preparing to castle. } 11... Bb7 { Black completes bishop development on b7, directing it toward the centre. } 12. O-O { White castles kingside. The remaining choices concern middlegame plans and piece activity; other playable opening continuations also exist. } *

