9. Qd8+ $3 { The checking queen offer draws the king to d8. The bishop on d2 still blocks the rook, which is why the king can legally accept it. } 9... Kxd8 { The king takes the queen on d8. White now has a way to attack it with two pieces at once. } 10. Bg5+ { The bishop leaves d2 and checks along the diagonal to d8, uncovering a rook check on the d-file at the same time. Double check must be answered by a king move. } 10... Kc7 { The king escapes to c7 in the published mating continuation. Ke8 is the other legal retreat and is answered by Rd8 mate. } 11. Bd8# { The bishop returns to d8 with mate, protected along the file by the rook. This demonstrates the finish after the resignation recorded in contemporary accounts. } *

