1... Bb4+ { Black moves the bishop from c5 to b4, changing its reach and coordinating with the remaining pieces. This gives check, so the opponent must first answer the attack on the king. } 2. Kd1 { White brings the king to d1. In a reduced ending the king can support a passer or restrict the opposing king. } 2... Bxe1 { Black captures the rook on e1. White can recapture the bishop with the king, but Black has won a rook for a bishop: a gain of the exchange, not a free rook. } *

